# Request cost (compute · egress · scale)

Before freezing data, caching, or serving lists, ask how the **hot path** behaves under load—not only what the UI shows.

## Check every read path

1. **DB egress** — Does one page view pull a whole blob / full table when it only needs a page?
2. **Compute** — Parse/serialize cost on Vercel and Cloudflare Workers for that payload size.
3. **Scaling** — What happens at 10× voters/games/traffic? Same pattern still cheap?

## Prefer

- Normalized rows + `LIMIT`/`OFFSET` (or keyset) for **any** list that can grow
- Small meta rows; join catalog tables when freeze immutability allows
- Client receives only the page it renders
- Same pagination rules on host/admin/settings reads as on public boards

## Avoid

- Fat `jsonb` (or equivalent) snapshots that force full read+parse per request just to slice in memory
- “Pagination in the UI” that still loads everything server-side
- Unbounded list queries (“load all, hosts will scroll”) on any surface

